  "id": "ENT120",
  "title": "The Community Noticeboard’s Empty Square",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "positive public good",
  "premise": "A neighborhood noticeboard fills with competing oversized announcements, hiding a small request for spare drawing paper. A volunteer gives each notice an equal marked square and reserves one clearly labeled REQUESTS area; the final square receives a bundle of donated blank paper and a tiny original thank-you sketch.",
  "hook": "The smallest request is under the largest headline.",
  "visible_action": "Posters overlap; grid lines appear; notices shrink into equal cells; paper request becomes visible; blank sheets arrive in a nearby collection tray.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A shared information space can make modest requests visible.",
  "gate": "Use fictional notices and no personal contact data; equal visual space is a story choice, not a complete moderation or public-policy solution.",
